{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/461919-potpurri-pantheon","id":461919,"title":"Potpurri Pantheon","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-29T23:43:35-07:00","id":461919,"title":"Potpurri Pantheon","content":"Has anyone experimented with a Pantheon made up of the gods of other Pantheons? Perhaps the Titan's escape was fought by the gods, but the gods lost many in the war and so they decided to gather together. Or else some broke free of their families and have decided to remain together as one Pantheon. The end result being a singular Pantheon built of gods from multiple Pantheons.<br /> Would there be a unique PSP? Or would the PSP be that of the Pantheon the majority of this conglomeration belonged to beforehand?<br /> Would they make their own Overworld/Underworld or would they just move into someone else's?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T01:04:38-07:00","id":461991,"title":"","content":"I've had Hera move to the Aesir (long story) but not a wholy new pantheon.<br /> <br /> I would imagine, though, that while they would eventually develop their own PSP it would not be soon. Not until their legend as a pantheon (as opposed to seperate members within it) had time to mature and grow. Unless the reason behind it was so epic and huge as to necessitate one being assigned, in a way, by Fate. In either case it would be different than any of the original ones, I would think. Either as their old ones were slowly replaced by the new overall theme of the pantheon or as a rather unsubtle 'rip and strip' as Fate shoves a bunch of survivor-gods into a whole new role they didn't necessarily ask for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T07:13:41-07:00","id":463482,"title":"","content":"The overall move of 2e is away from Pantheons being clans, in the Vampire sense, to metaphysical and cultural lineages within Fate. They're not necessarily exclusive, either - Isis and Hermes really get around, mythologically speaking, and there's the <i>interpretatio </i>phenomenon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T08:18:00-07:00","id":463571,"title":"","content":"That sounds very interesting, indeed. Thanks for that, Neall. I like that idea. I assume that this will also save the Roman/Greek Pantheon dilemma?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T08:20:19-07:00","id":463575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/461919-potpurri-pantheon?p=463571#post463571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds very interesting, indeed. Thanks for that, Neall. I like that idea. I assume that this will also save the Roman/Greek Pantheon dilemma?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, the Legend rules that allow gods to mantle different elements of their divinity does that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T08:47:54-07:00","id":463590,"title":"","content":"I have this mental image of Zeus running late to some kind of godly meeting, hurriedly getting dressed and rushing to make it on time only for Apollo to nudge him and whisper &quot;You have your Jove pants on, dude. Doesn't go with your Zeus sandals at <i>all</i>.&quot; and the other gods tittering and pointing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T09:08:47-07:00","id":463601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/461919-potpurri-pantheon?p=463575#post463575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nah, the Legend rules that allow gods to mantle different elements of their divinity does that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am now more excited to see how they will handle this than ever before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T12:45:02-07:00","id":463732,"title":"","content":"I find that really troubling, since it means one culture gets to have the &quot;real&quot; Gods and the other cultures get the &quot;fake&quot; Gods. Does this mean the Greeks were objectively <i>right</i> and only later did <i>their</i> Gods take on the persona of Etruscan and Roman Gods? Is that going to extend to the idea there is one, objective group of &quot;Native American&quot; Gods who &quot;mantle&quot; themselves into Apache, Comanche, Iroquois, Cherokee, Navajo and Inuit forms despite the fact that those cultures have less in common than the Russians, Norse, Greek, Irish and Sumerians?<br /> <br /> Yeah. That's really discouraging to hear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T12:52:13-07:00","id":463753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/461919-potpurri-pantheon?p=463732#post463732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find that really troubling, since it means one culture gets to have the &quot;real&quot; Gods and the other cultures get the &quot;fake&quot; Gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's not at all what that means. It means Zeus and Jupiter are probably the same guy and different cultural representations, not that Raven of the Tlingit, Kutkh, and Bran the Blessed are the same god. Don't make a mountain out of a molehill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 03-31-2015, 03:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T06:29:41-07:00","id":491599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/461919-potpurri-pantheon#post461919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anyone experimented with a Pantheon made up of the gods of other Pantheons?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ever heard of phoenician religion? It's pratically a historical version of this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}